            <ArticleTitle>Greater trochanteric pain syndrome diagnosis and treatment.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>279-89</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.pmr.2014.01.009</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S1047-9651(14)00010-2</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Lateral hip pain, or greater trochanteric pain syndrome, is a commonly seen condition; in this article, the relevant anatomy, epidemiology, and evaluation strategies of greater trochanteric pain syndrome are reviewed. Specific attention is focused on imaging of this syndrome and treatment techniques, including ultrasound-guided interventions.</AbstractText>
